{"availability":"available","full":"diegomanuel/binance-to-google-sheets","name":"binance-to-google-sheets","description":"Google Spreadsheets add-on to get data directly from Binance API without any intermediaries! :rocket:","category":"Developer tools","language":"JavaScript","stars":436,"forks":72,"created":"2020-11-02T10:13:11Z","updated":"2024-05-03T22:06:07Z","license":"GPL-3.0","branch":"master","homepage":"","topics":["binance-api","bitcoin","cryptocurrency-exchanges","financial-data","google-spreadsheets","trade"],"demo":"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1AcOcPFsncrDB_ve3wWMHwfiFql6A4hmG1sFc01LLTDg/edit#gid=1522299933","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-05T21:33:13.792Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-05T21:33:13.792Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-05T21:33:13.792Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-05T21:33:13.792Z","stars":436,"forks":72}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A lightweight Google Spreadsheets Add-On to GET data directly from Binance API without any intermediaries!","Since Binance decided to block API requests coming from restricted countries like USA (from which the Google servers in where our spreadsheets run are located), you'll probably need a proxy. Check Binance to Google Sheets Add-On Proxy for a basic proxy server implementation that I did for myself and is currently working fine. It may be useful for you too! See the README.md for further details.","This add-on is basically an API client specially hand-crafted to work between Google Spreadsheets and Binance. By using the BINANCE() formula in your spreadsheet, you can get data fetched from Binance API like:"],"features":["Current market prices","Historical market OHLCV","Total account assets from Binance wallets (SPOT + EARN + CROSS + ISOLATED + FUTURES + SUB-ACCOUNTS)","All current open orders (SPOT + CROSS + ISOLATED + FUTURES)","Latest done/finished orders (SPOT + CROSS + ISOLATED + FUTURES)"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/diegomanuel/binance-to-google-sheets/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"ccda7163a2f57a1155fbf4e7bfedeeefb1da66a375b3aa994d9d5a94b7e43c25","extractedAt":"2026-10-05T21:33:13.899Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-05T21:33:13.899Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A lightweight Google Spreadsheets Add-On to GET data directly from Binance API without any intermediaries!","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/diegomanuel/binance-to-google-sheets/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[{"text":"Since Binance decided to block API requests coming from restricted countries like USA (from which the Google servers in where our spreadsheets run are located), you'll probably need a proxy. Check Binance to Google Sheets Add-On Proxy for a basic proxy server implementation that I did for myself and is currently working fine. It may be useful for you too! See the README.md for…","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/diegomanuel/binance-to-google-sheets/blob/master/README.md"}],"requirements":[{"kind":"api_key","status":"not_required","text":"At first glance, NO Binance API key is needed to call public endpoints like current prices, historic prices and 24h stats.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/diegomanuel/binance-to-google-sheets/blob/master/README.md"},{"kind":"api_key","status":"required","text":"It only requires a Binance API key for private endpoints like account info and open/done/table orders, but a READ-ONLY API key is enough for everything to work.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/diegomanuel/binance-to-google-sheets/blob/master/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"It only requires a Binance API key for private endpoints like account info and open/done/table orders, but a READ-ONLY API key is enough for everything to work.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/diegomanuel/binance-to-google-sheets/blob/master/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Clone the repo and login to your Google account with clasp by running: clasp login.","sourceU